            "heading": "3. Differentiation of a Determinant",
            "headingHinglish": "3. Differentiation of a Determinant",
            "body": "If Δ(x) is a determinant whose entries are differentiable functions of x, then **Δ'(x)** is obtained by **differentiating ONE row (or one column) at a time** and summing all n determinants:\nFor a 3 × 3 determinant with rows R₁(x), R₂(x), R₃(x):\n**Δ'(x) = det([ R₁' ; R₂ ; R₃ ]) + det([ R₁ ; R₂' ; R₃ ]) + det([ R₁ ; R₂ ; R₃' ])**!\n*(Shortcut: If two rows are constants, you only need to differentiate the ONE variable row!)*",
            "bodyHinglish": "If Δ(x) is a determinant whose entries are differentiable functions of x, then **Δ'(x)** is obtained by **differentiating ONE row (or one column) at a time** and summing all n determinants:\nFor a 3 × 3 determinant with rows R₁(x), R₂(x), R₃(x):\n**Δ'(x) = det([ R₁' ; R₂ ; R₃ ]) + det([ R₁ ; R₂' ; R₃ ]) + det([ R₁ ; R₂ ; R₃' ])**!\n*(Shortcut: If two rows are constants, you only need to differentiate the ONE variable row!)*"
