            "body": "If f: [a, b] → [f(a), f(b)] is strictly increasing and continuous, then the area under y = f(x) (vertical strips) PLUS the area to the left of x = f⁻¹(y) (horizontal strips) fills the exact difference of two rectangles:\n\n**∫ₐᵇ f(x) dx  +  ∫_(f(a))^(f(b)) f⁻¹(y) dy  =  b · f(b) − a · f(a)**!",
            "bodyHinglish": "If f: [a, b] → [f(a), f(b)] is strictly increasing and continuous, then the area under y = f(x) (vertical strips) PLUS the area to the left of x = f⁻¹(y) (horizontal strips) fills the exact difference of two rectangles:\n\n**∫ₐᵇ f(x) dx  +  ∫_(f(a))^(f(b)) f⁻¹(y) dy  =  b · f(b) − a · f(a)**!"
