            "heading": "3. Method 3: Linear First-Order Differential Equations (100% Exam Favourite!)",
            "headingHinglish": "3. Method 3: Linear First-Order Differential Equations (100% Exam Favourite!)",
            "body": "### Type A (Linear in y): **dy/dx + P(x) · y = Q(x)**\n1. Make sure coefficient of dy/dx is **+1**!\n2. Compute **Integrating Factor: IF = e^(∫ P(x) dx)** (remember: **e^(k ln x) = xᵏ**!).\n3. General solution: **y · (IF) = ∫ [ Q(x) · (IF) ] dx + C**!\n\n### Type B (Linear in x — When Type A Fails!): **dx/dy + P(y) · x = Q(y)**\n1. Compute **IF = e^(∫ P(y) dy)**.\n2. General solution: **x · (IF) = ∫ [ Q(y) · (IF) ] dy + C**!",
            "bodyHinglish": "### Type A (Linear in y): **dy/dx + P(x) · y = Q(x)**\n1. Make sure coefficient of dy/dx is **+1**!\n2. Compute **Integrating Factor: IF = e^(∫ P(x) dx)** (remember: **e^(k ln x) = xᵏ**!).\n3. General solution: **y · (IF) = ∫ [ Q(x) · (IF) ] dx + C**!\n\n### Type B (Linear in x — When Type A Fails!): **dx/dy + P(y) · x = Q(y)**\n1. Compute **IF = e^(∫ P(y) dy)**.\n2. General solution: **x · (IF) = ∫ [ Q(y) · (IF) ] dy + C**!"
