            "body": "Prem ne shehar ke naye highway interchange par do flyover ramps dekhe: ek ramp East-West ja raha tha aur doosra uske upar se North-South nikal raha tha. Dono ramps na parallel the, na hi ek-doosre ko kahin touch kar rahe the! 2D mein do non-parallel lines hamesha milti hain, par 3D mein aisi lines ko **skew lines** kehte hain — aur unke beech ka vertical clearance (shortest distance) engineers ke liye sabse zaroori calculation hota hai!",
            "bodyHinglish": "Prem ne shehar ke naye highway interchange par do flyover ramps dekhe: ek ramp East-West ja raha tha aur doosra uske upar se North-South nikal raha tha. Dono ramps na parallel the, na hi ek-doosre ko kahin touch kar rahe the! 2D mein do non-parallel lines hamesha milti hain, par 3D mein aisi lines ko **skew lines** kehte hain — aur unke beech ka vertical clearance (shortest distance) engineers ke liye sabse zaroori calculation hota hai!"
