            "heading": "Introduction",
            "headingHinglish": "Introduction",
            "body": "Ranjana apne dost ke saath Ludo khel rahi thi aur do dice phenke. Pehla die table par ruk gaya aur us par **5** aaya, jabki doosra die abhi ghoom raha tha! Ranjana ko jeetne ke liye total sum kam se kam **9** chahiye. Normally do dice mein sum ≥ 9 ki probability 10/36 = 5/18 hoti hai — par ab jab humein pata chal chuka hai ki pehla die **5** hai, toh sample space 36 se sikud kar sirf 6 outcomes ((5,1) se (5,6)) reh gaya, aur sum ≥ 9 ke liye (5,4), (5,5), (5,6) — yaani **3/6 = 1/2** chance! Is tarah nayi jaankari milne par probability ka update hona hi **Conditional Probability** kehlata hai!\n\nClass 11 ke [Probability](../../../class11/maths/probability/probability.md) mein tumne sample space, events, aur addition theorem seekha tha — ab hum usi par Class 12 ke powerful tools build karenge.",
            "bodyHinglish": "Ranjana apne dost ke saath Ludo khel rahi thi aur do dice phenke. Pehla die table par ruk gaya aur us par **5** aaya, jabki doosra die abhi ghoom raha tha! Ranjana ko jeetne ke liye total sum kam se kam **9** chahiye. Normally do dice mein sum ≥ 9 ki probability 10/36 = 5/18 hoti hai — par ab jab humein pata chal chuka hai ki pehla die **5** hai, toh sample space 36 se sikud kar sirf 6 outcomes ((5,1) se (5,6)) reh gaya, aur sum ≥ 9 ke liye (5,4), (5,5), (5,6) — yaani **3/6 = 1/2** chance! Is tarah nayi jaankari milne par probability ka update hona hi **Conditional Probability** kehlata hai!\n\nClass 11 ke [Probability](../../../class11/maths/probability/probability.md) mein tumne sample space, events, aur addition theorem seekha tha — ab hum usi par Class 12 ke powerful tools build karenge."
